# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# ORDER MATTERS — the /assets/* rule must come before the SPA catch-all.
#
# Missing hashed assets MUST 404, never fall into the SPA catch-all:
# real files are served before redirects run, so this rule only fires
# for /assets URLs that no longer exist (a previous build's chunks).
# Without it, a service worker installing across a deploy boundary gets
# 200 + index.html for its dead precache URLs, "successfully" caches
# HTML under .js paths, and activates — every load then throws the
# MIME-type chunk error and the "Updating PokerGrid" overlay loops,
# because the self-heal ladder only escalates to a purge when an
# install FAILS. An honest 404 makes the poisoned install fail, which
# both prevents the bad cache and lets the recovery escalate.
/assets/* /404.html 404

# SPA catch-all: every app route serves the shell.
/* /index.html 200
